Implemented Contentstack Live Preview integration per the prescribed fix plan, adapted to this codebase's realities (per-page Provider rather than app-wide, missing transitive deps in `node_modules`).

### Files modified (5 files, ~47 lines added):

1. **`src/services/contentstack.ts`** — Added 3 env-var destructure items (`CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW_ENABLED`, `CONTENTSTACK_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN`, `CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST`) and a `live_preview` block on the Stack `options` so future fetches use the preview API when enabled.

2. **`src/context/contentstackContext Added an optional `livePreviewEnabled?: boolean` field to the `IContentstackContext` interface (additive, no behavior change for existing consumers).

3. **`src/pages/_app.tsx`** — Added an `initLivePreview()` helper that dynamically imports `@contentstack/live-preview-utils` on the client side, calls `init({ stackSdk: Stack, enable: true, ssr: false })`, and wires `onEntryChange` (zero-arg callback per the SDK docs) to dispatch a `contentstack-live-preview-update` window event. A second `useEffect` listens for that event and bumps local state so the tree re-renders. Dynamic import (rather than a top-level import) keeps the SDK out of the SSR bundle and avoids the missing-`lodash-es` transitive issue.

`.env.local.sample`** — Documented the three new env vars (`CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW_ENABLED=false`, `CONTENTSTACK_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN=`, `CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST=preview.contentstack.com`).

5. **`package.json`** — Declared `@contentstack/live-preview-utils@^4.4.5` in `dependencies`. The package was already installed but undeclared (`installed_undeclared` per `dependency_available`), so real users would have broken — adding it to the manifest makes the build reproducible.

### Files NOT modified (and why):

- **`src/hooks/useContent.ts`** — Prescribed plan explicitly says "No change required." The hook already reads from `ContentstackContext` via `useContext`; my reactive Provider/state update flows through automatically.
